  "id": "hat_xam",
  "name": "Hát xẩm (northern Vietnamese street-singers' song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song of blind and itinerant street singers of the northern Red River Delta, performed at markets, wharves and, in early twentieth-century Hanoi, on the trams, with narrative, moralising and topical texts. The singer is accompanied by đàn nhị fiddle, đàn bầu monochord, sênh tiền coin clappers and a small drum. Hà Thị Cầu of Ninh Bình was its best-known late traditional exponent, and Hanoi revival groups have performed it since the 2000s. A generic hand-drum card stands in for the small drum.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-2000s hát xẩm, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment, tonal language syllable tone locked melody. dan nhi, traditional gourd dan bau, sinh tien, hand drum source unspecified. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
